Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:52:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] practice: download the attachment through the documented
 v3 endpoint

A real session's attachment url is https://app.devin.ai/attachments/<uuid>/activity.html,
a browser page that answers 401 without a user session; _download fetched it
without authentication and failed.

- The UUID comes from attachment_id, or from the path of that app.devin.ai
  link; the name must be activity.html. The link itself is never fetched.
- GET https://api.devin.ai/v3/organizations/{org}/attachments/{uuid}/activity.html
  with the service key, as documented; its redirect Location is checked by
  the existing allowlist and public-address check and fetched without the
  Authorization header, with the existing size bound and no further redirect.
- Tests: the official endpoint is used with the key, app.devin.ai is never
  requested, redirects outside the allowlist or to a private address are
  refused, and no other host ever receives Authorization.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
